# OS
.DS_Store

# Secrets
ignore/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. An unanchored `data/` also matches
# src/eval/data/, which config.EVAL_DATA_DIR documents as the *committed*
# counterpart holding the LLM recordings an evaluation replays - a fresh clone
# cannot reproduce the report's figures without them (found during U6).
#
# The trained rent model is the one exception (U9.1): it is small (~140 KB),
# has no license restriction (it's derived weights, not the Kaggle corpus
# itself), and committing it means a fresh clone can run the pipeline without
# a training pass. Everything else under data/ - the source CSVs, the Chroma
# index, the checkpoint DB, the LLM cache - stays out. Git can't re-include a
# file inside an ignored directory, so the exclusion has to be re-stated one
# level at a time down to the file.
/data/*
!/data/processed/
/data/processed/*
!/data/processed/rent_model.joblib

# Docs
docs/private/
claude.md
CLAUDE.md

